===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|haira-|lang=ang}} from {{proto|Indo-European|kei-||koi-|lang=ang}}. Cognate with Old Saxon {{term|her|hēr|lang=osx}}, Old High German {{term|her|hēr|lang=goh}} (German {{term|hehr||august, holy|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|hárr||grey|lang=non}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ha:ɹ/|lang=ang}}

===Adjective===
{{infl|ang|adjective|head=hār}}

